timecrate (3.0.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The quarterly capstone decrypts the kit on disk instead of /tmp, which
    is a small tmpfs on Ubuntu 26.04, and fails when the kit is not
    authenticated or does not extract whole, instead of passing it as
    unsigned. A missing package sample, package selections or desktop
    settings fail the run too. The guest reboots itself for the reboot
    check, a forced stop and start tells a guest that cannot boot from a
    hypervisor that lost track of it, and the alert lists every failure.

 -- Norvi <apt@globalentry.systems>  Sun, 04 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

timecrate (3.0.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * First public release, under the name Timecrate. Kits written by earlier
    versions are read, verified, restored and pruned as one series with new
    ones. Alerts go to a command of your choice, include lines may be globs,
    and the timers are enabled on installation and kept across upgrades.

 -- Norvi <apt@globalentry.systems>  Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
